{
 "uid": "backup-restore",
 "title": "Backup & Restore \u2014 objects come back, data does not",
 "schemaVersion": 39,
 "tags": [
  "backup",
  "restore",
  "operations",
  "storage"
 ],
 "time": {
  "from": "now-30m",
  "to": "now"
 },
 "refresh": "30s",
 "editable": true,
 "graphTooltip": 1,
 "annotations": {
  "list": []
 },
 "templating": {
  "list": []
 },
 "panels": [
  {
   "title": "What this drill looks like on a graph",
   "type": "text",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 5,
    "w": 24,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "Run the drill with this open. Two things happen, and only one of them is a recovery.\n\n**Objects come back.** Deleting the restore marker drops the ConfigMap count; applying the archive puts it straight back. That line returning to where it started is what a manifest backup guarantees.\n\n**Data does not.** The PVC is a claim, not the disk. Delete it and restore, and the claim returns bound to a *different* volume: the `volumename` on the right changes, and the volume's age below resets to zero. A brand-new empty disk. Nothing that was on the old one is in the archive, and nothing here brings it back \u2014 that needs a volume snapshot or Velero with restic."
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Objects in the namespace \u2014 what the archive restores",
   "type": "timeseries",
   "description": "The dip is your simulated loss; the step back up is the restore. These are the kinds backup.sh captures.",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 9,
    "w": 14,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 5
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "none",
     "min": 0,
     "custom": {
      "drawStyle": "line",
      "lineWidth": 2,
      "fillOpacity": 12,
      "stacking": {
       "mode": "none"
      },
      "spanNulls": false
     }
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "legend": {
     "displayMode": "list",
     "placement": "bottom",
     "showLegend": true
    },
    "tooltip": {
     "mode": "multi",
     "sort": "none"
    }
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "count(kube_configmap_info{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\"}) or vector(0)",
     "legendFormat": "ConfigMaps",
     "refId": "A"
    },
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "count(kube_secret_info{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\"}) or vector(0)",
     "legendFormat": "Secrets",
     "refId": "B"
    },
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "count(kube_deployment_created{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\"}) or vector(0)",
     "legendFormat": "Deployments",
     "refId": "C"
    },
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "count(kube_service_info{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\"}) or vector(0)",
     "legendFormat": "Services",
     "refId": "D"
    },
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "count(kube_persistentvolumeclaim_info{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\"}) or vector(0)",
     "legendFormat": "PVCs",
     "refId": "E"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "The claim and the volume behind it",
   "type": "table",
   "description": "The PVC name survives the round-trip. The volumename does not: a restored claim is provisioned a new, empty volume, and that identity change is the data loss.",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 9,
    "w": 10,
    "x": 14,
    "y": 5
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "custom": {
      "align": "left"
     }
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "showHeader": true
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "kube_persistentvolumeclaim_info{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\"}",
     "instant": true,
     "format": "table",
     "refId": "A"
    }
   ],
   "transformations": [
    {
     "id": "organize",
     "options": {
      "excludeByName": {
       "Time": true,
       "Value": true,
       "__name__": true,
       "container": true,
       "endpoint": true,
       "instance": true,
       "job": true,
       "pod": true,
       "service": true,
       "namespace": true,
       "uid": true
      },
      "renameByName": {
       "persistentvolumeclaim": "claim",
       "volumename": "bound volume",
       "storageclass": "storage class",
       "volumemode": "mode"
      }
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Age of the volume behind the claim \u2014 zero means it is new",
   "type": "timeseries",
   "description": "A restored claim is not the old disk. This is the age of the PersistentVolume currently bound to restore-data: it climbs while the data survives, and drops to zero the moment a restore provisions a replacement. Bytes-used is deliberately not plotted \u2014 on local-path storage the kubelet reports the node's filesystem, not the claim.",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 8,
    "w": 12,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 14
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "s",
     "min": 0,
     "custom": {
      "drawStyle": "line",
      "lineWidth": 2,
      "fillOpacity": 12,
      "stacking": {
       "mode": "none"
      },
      "spanNulls": false
     }
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "legend": {
     "displayMode": "list",
     "placement": "bottom",
     "showLegend": true
    },
    "tooltip": {
     "mode": "multi",
     "sort": "none"
    }
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "(time() - kube_persistentvolume_created) * on(persistentvolume) group_left() (kube_persistentvolume_claim_ref{claim_namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\",name=\"restore-data\"})",
     "legendFormat": "bound volume age",
     "refId": "A"
    },
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "time() - kube_persistentvolumeclaim_created{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\",persistentvolumeclaim=\"restore-data\"}",
     "legendFormat": "claim age",
     "refId": "B"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Is the claim bound, and is the writer running?",
   "type": "timeseries",
   "description": "Between the delete and the restore both go to zero. A claim that stays Pending after a restore means no storage class could provision it \u2014 a different failure from data loss.",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 8,
    "w": 12,
    "x": 12,
    "y": 14
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "none",
     "min": 0,
     "custom": {
      "drawStyle": "line",
      "lineWidth": 2,
      "fillOpacity": 12,
      "stacking": {
       "mode": "none"
      },
      "spanNulls": false
     }
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "legend": {
     "displayMode": "list",
     "placement": "bottom",
     "showLegend": true
    },
    "tooltip": {
     "mode": "multi",
     "sort": "none"
    }
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "sum(kube_persistentvolumeclaim_status_phase{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\",persistentvolumeclaim=\"restore-data\",phase=\"Bound\"}) or vector(0)",
     "legendFormat": "claim bound",
     "refId": "A"
    },
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "sum(kube_deployment_status_replicas_available{namespace=\"{{.WorkloadNamespace}}\",deployment=\"data-writer\"}) or vector(0)",
     "legendFormat": "data-writer replicas available",
     "refId": "B"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
